WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.820
- Every minute right now on LinkedIn,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:06.110
almost 200 people join,
9,000 connections are made,

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.110
almost six people get a job every minute

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.650
out of 4,500 applications
that occur every minute.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.160
- And every minute,

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:16.403
1 billion LinkedIn notifications
are sent to your inbox.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.970
Okay, I joke kinda

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.560
but you know what's
having a moment right now?

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.393
LinkedIn.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.140
You're almost hitting two
years at LinkedIn as CEO,

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.560
happy almost work anniversary.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.340
What is different now at LinkedIn
than it was two years ago.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.370
- It's been fascinating
to lead the company

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.630
over the last couple
of years through COVID,

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.530
through a great talent reshuffle.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.050
Where professionals across the world

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.130
are not only rethinking
where and how they work,

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.750
but why they work

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.920
and the whole world is turning
to LinkedIn these days.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.160
- [Joanna] Of course, that's
exactly what you'd expect

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.110
the CEO of LinkedIn to say

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.480
but I have to admit lately,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.650
I've also been turning to LinkedIn

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.970
and not because I'm looking for a new job

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.130
but because the other
social networks I use

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.880
have all sorts of issues.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.380
- I started Facebook, I run it

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.213
and at the end of the day

00:01:08.213 --> 00:01:10.490
I'm responsible for what happens here.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.780
- We weren't expecting any of this

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.780
when we created Twitter over 12 years ago.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.060
- LinkedIn has largely dodged
the social media backlash.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.210
Why do you think that is?

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.780
- What it's all about on LinkedIn

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.770
is connection for opportunity.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.150
It's about people who are
having conversations around

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:27.180
trying to get a job or trying to hire

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.770
or trying to learn a new skill,

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.480
maybe trying to buy or sell a new product.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.220
Maybe trying to start a new company.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.700
- [Joanna] Basically people
act a lot less like a jerk

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.930
when they're trying to network for work

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.360
or when they're looking
for, as he puts it.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.340
- Economic opportunity, economic
opportunity, opportunity

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.670
economic opportunities, opportunity.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.590
- So while LinkedIn may
have long been known

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:49.940
as the most uncool social network.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.740
It's actually one of the most civilized

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.780
and useful social networks

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.780
and not only for us
old-seasoned professionals

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.540
- We're seeing a lot of Gen-Z
join the network right now.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.250
They're much more interested
in portraying themselves

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:09.210
through video or through
a much more robust profile

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:10.850
than maybe older generations.

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:12.590
So we're seeing the platform evolve

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.220
to much more cater to them.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.850
- So how is the platform changing

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.810
to respond to the influx of younger users?

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.980
With new features that stand to modernize

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:24.660
and get you using the 18 year
old professional network more?

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.280
The feature I found the most interesting

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.200
and wanna see come to
other social networks.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.270
Is a no politics button,
it wipes politics news

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.210
or chatter from your main feed.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.270
How does the system
decide what's political?

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.410
- Through our editorial team,

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.160
through our semantic classifiers,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.060
through what the
community tells us they do

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.200
or they don't want.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.930
We're just constantly trying to figure out

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:43.840
the types of content

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.780
that make the most sense for them to see.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:49.530
- You guys are testing it right
now, small amount of people.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:52.430
Do you plan to roll this out
more broadly and if so when?

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:55.330
- Yeah absolutely, I would
love to see how people use it.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.830
If they find it effective,

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.750
if it's helping them better accomplish

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.530
what they're trying to
accomplish on LinkedIn

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.830
and then if that makes sense,
we'll roll it out to more.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:05.050
- You can check now to see
if you have this setting.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.140
Go to account preferences,
feed preferences,

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.530
there you might see a toggle

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:12.350
asking if you'd like to see
political content in your feed.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.440
I haven't seen any
political posts in my feed

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.410
since enabling it but to be honest,

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.460
I didn't have a ton to start with.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.293
In the coming months,

00:03:19.293 --> 00:03:21.710
you'll also be able to launch a live audio

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.980
or video event right on LinkedIn.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:25.550
Think clubhouse and zoom

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.720
right in the LinkedIn app or website.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.100
- Especially through the pandemic

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.180
we saw a ton of events
that moved on to LinkedIn.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:34.320
Obviously, professional events
you can't have in person.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:37.180
Then a lot of what we're
seeing work on LinkedIn

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.960
are things like career
fairs that you couldn't,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.720
you know, kinda do in person

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.490
or the small professional
events in webinars.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.730
- [Joanna] You can now also add video

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.370
to your profile photo.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.560
In the mobile app, tap your profile photo,

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.260
then tap add cover story

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:54.130
and you can introduce yourself
with a 30 second video.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.780
- Gen-Z really wants to
be showcasing themselves

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.060
through video first.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.910
It's not just about filling
out texts on their profile,

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.870
it's constantly sharing what
they're doing, what they know,

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:06.410
how they do it, how they
know it, through video.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.460
- [Joanna] And just like
every other social network.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.820
LinkedIn is trying to attract creators.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.020
People who make content with new tools

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.730
that let you reach bigger
audiences on LinkedIn,

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.040
but Roslansky says it's more
than just sharing to go viral.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.850
- Oftentimes, you know,

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.720
you think about creation
for entertainment's sake.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.010
There's also creation for opportunity,

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.760
which is I have these things

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.410
that I wanna be able to teach my network

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.060
and I'm gonna find an
interesting creative way

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:33.430
to showcase that on LinkedIn.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.940
- Is there a compensation
model for creators on LinkedIn?

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:40.800
- So we've actually taken a
small group of people where,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.690
you know, kind of compensating
them more than anything

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.250
for their knowledge of like,
hey, what are you seeing

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.930
and learning across LinkedIn

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.020
that we should take into consideration

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.940
as we think about building
features for the masses

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:55.440
- He's talking about LinkedIn's
Creator accelerator Program.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.220
A $25 million fund,
that's going to creators

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.180
to help them build their
audience on the platform

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.790
and finally, I couldn't
let the LinkedIn CEO go

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:07.320
without asking about
everyone's top LinkedIn peeves.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.860
First it's the LinkedIn website,

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.810
kind of a mess and cluttered.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.420
- Thank you very much for the feedback.

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.890
Absolutely something we're working on.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:17.150
- For the record, that's what
LinkedIn told me in 2016,

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.310
when I complained about the same thing.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:23.120
The next is a lot of
notification and emails.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.290
- We really wanna put control
in the hands of the members

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:28.820
for what they do or don't
wanna get notified about.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.020
You can literally turn on or off

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:32.110
anything that you wanna know about

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.520
and I think it's really
important to understand

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.770
that you have a ton of people right now

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.680
who are trying to say,

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:40.200
hey, any time a new job
is posted on LinkedIn

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.600
that hits these criteria,
please notify me immediately.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.820
- You can go into settings, communications

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.980
and get very specific about what you do

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.750
and don't wanna be notified about

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:54.210
and then last spam in messages.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.790
- So again, something where
you can always, you know,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.420
decide to turn InMail off.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.780
If you want you can decide

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.230
I only wanna hear from my network

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.920
and we are testing a
variety of a kinda new UI

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:05.780
and relevance models there

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.620
that I think they're gonna
create a much cleaner inbox

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:08.453
for people on LinkedIn.

00:06:08.453 --> 00:06:11.150
- But really how does the CEO of LinkedIn

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.420
celebrate a work anniversary?

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.470
- You know, I haven't hit
that two year anniversary yet,

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:17.470
so I'll let you know.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:20.353
I'm sure you'll be notified
when I do with that anniversary.

